What the support desk knows, kept next to the code that knows it. One desk, every product:
`sched-prod` (calendar invites for about 300k people) and the rest. When something breaks, the reports land here first.

For #4471, start with the [signed incident review](/kb/incidents/4471-review), which separates
the exported classifier groups, disputed reports, and current public tracking.

<Callout kind="warn">
The <a href="/kb/triage/dedupe">triage guide</a> is under review: matching subjects and matching classifier buckets
do not independently establish shared causation. Read its review notice before relying on the historical
instructions. <a href="/kb/decisions/0002-evidence-based-triage">Decision 0002</a> proposes a replacement;
it is not adopted, and decision 0001 remains the accepted record.
</Callout>

Document status is not product status. An accepted decision records approval of a policy; it does
not establish that every report shares one cause or that a fix shipped. Review warnings and
incident evidence still matter.

